<title>UK: BOE GIVES UK MONEY MARKET 730 MLN STG FURTHER HELP.</title>
<headline>BOE GIVES UK MONEY MARKET 730 MLN STG FURTHER HELP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 730 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 155 million stg in bills outright and 575 million stg in repos to August 26 and 27.</p>
<p>The Bank has provided liquidity totalling 1.148 billion stg in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.3 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
